# Motion

Authored motion uses the `--motion-*` tokens in `src/shared/styles/tokens.css` and recipes in `src/shared/motion/motionSystem.ts`. Documented in `specs/tokens/token-reference.md`.

- Durations, easings, springs, distances, scales, fades, and stagger come from those variables / recipes.
- Do not add a raw duration or a `cubic-bezier()` outside `tokens.css`.
- `linear` is allowed only for real time (spinner, loading pulse, countdown, progress) and for the damped error shake. Loading pulse duration is `--motion-duration-pulse`.
- `--motion-ease-ios` is reached only through `--motion-nav-*`, `--motion-sheet-*`, `--motion-dialog-*`, and `--motion-modal-*`. Do not put it on components.
- Page push/pop uses `--motion-nav-enter-*` / `--motion-nav-exit-*` and `--motion-nav-parallax` (Android 32px, iOS 30%). Do not invent a separate page transition.
- Fades use `--motion-fade-in*` / `--motion-fade-out*` / `--motion-cross-fade*`.
- `--motion-spring-bouncy` is one confirmed-success element per screen. Errors do not bounce.
- Reduced motion swaps travel for a fade at `--motion-duration-sm` and `--motion-ease-standard` (or the fade recipes). It does not delete feedback. Stagger, parallax, and shake are removed.
- Do not animate height, width, or `left` / `top`. Use transform and opacity.
